SD-patch 0015: desktop cold-start batch 1 — defer the two heaviest import
chains off the Gateway/AgentServer startup critical paths.

Measurements that motivated this patch (f23-instr packaged install,
2026-11-01, hot-restart rounds R1/R2, `-X importtime` on the bundled
jw venv):

- AgentServer: `from jiuwenswarm.server.agent_ws_server import ...`
  costs 10.7s on a warm tree; 82% of it (8.73s) is the
  `agents.harness.code.rails.heartbeat.runtime` chain pulled by a
  single module-top import in agent_ws_server.py (line 28). The
  runtime object is only needed after the first Gateway connection;
  0010 already gated its *start* behind that connection but left the
  *import* on the module-top critical path.
- Gateway: `from jiuwenswarm.gateway.channel_manager.channel_manager
  import ChannelManager` (inside `_run`) transitively executes
  `channel_manager/__init__.py`, which eagerly imports nine IM-platform
  connect modules (telegram/slack/discord/xiaoyi/dingtalk/whatsapp/
  wecom/wechat, ~7.4s incl. their SDKs: telegram, slack_bolt+aiohttp,
  discord, redis, opentelemetry). The desktop build only ever uses the
  WebChannel; every IM platform is already imported lazily inside its
  enabled-branch in app_gateway.py, so the eager package __init__ is
  pure dead weight on the critical path.
- ImageModalityWarmup blocked the AgentServer event loop for 4.3s
  right after listen (hot-restart R2: port listening 12:31:31.85,
  Gateway handshake 12:31:37.37): `_build_probe_models` synchronously
  imports `agent_adapter.interface_deep` (the multi-second openjiuwen
  model-factory chain) and builds Model objects on the loop, so the
  first ws handshake queued behind it. The import+build now runs in a
  worker thread before the probe round, matching the pattern 0010
  established for the checkpointer warmup.

Changes:
- server/agent_ws_server.py: the module-top HeartbeatRailRuntime
  import moves to the two first-use sites (server construction
  heartbeat wiring, and the two runtime touch points that may run
  before that wiring on an already-constructed server). The heavy
  chain now loads while the ws port is already listening.
- gateway/channel_manager/__init__.py: the nine IM-platform +
  WebChannel eager imports become lazy (PEP 562 module __getattr__
  + explicit re-export shims), same technique 0010 applied to
  gateway/__init__.py. `from ...channel_manager.channel_manager
  import ChannelManager` and every direct sub-module import stop
  triggering the IM SDK chain.
- server/runtime/image_modality_warmup.py: `_build_probe_models`
  (interface_deep import + Model construction) executes in a worker
  thread via asyncio.to_thread; the loop-side await keeps the probe
  round async and the handshake window free of sync work.

Additional measurement (dev tree, hot pyc, importtime, after the
full change set incl. the call_timeout_patch move):
- agent_ws_server import: 24.5s -> 3.46s (depth-1 remainder: hook_event
  1.15s event bus + openjiuwen logging 0.63s + small utils — the
  patch-layer floor).
- channel_manager package __init__: 7.37s -> 0.19s.
- app_gateway total: 21.5s -> 3.4s.
Expected effect on the packaged tree (measured on dev tree, hot pyc;
the packaged tree historically tracks these within ~15%):
AGENT-READY 33.5-34s -> ~20-22s.

